experiment: hcsweep
  instrument        hcsweep   trial seed 0000000001356b97   1214 trials per arm
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  hcsweep -- is there an operating point where the GESTURE and the
  LESSON both work? The gesture is free and replicated; the lesson is
  free and measured; at the one point where the gesture was tuned, the
  lesson keeps only a fifth of its strength.
  the axis      `halfcenter_drive` (Matsuoka's S), gain HELD at 0.45. The
                gain axis was swept first and refused; it named this axis
                as its own overturning condition, because the oscillating
                window is bounded and mapped in drive, not in gain.
  the quantity  per drive, TWO numbers: error early-minus-late on a FIXED
                target (the lesson), and the phase separation with its
                share (the gesture). Both have to be read or the trade is
                invisible.
  the bar       UNCHANGED from the gain sweep: some drive must give a
                lesson drop over HALF of the half-centre-off reference
                0.2197 -- that is 0.1099 -- while keeping sep > 10 Hz and
                share in 0.15-0.85. At gain 0.45 the lesson ALREADY
                clears it (+0.1243); only sep falls short, at 8.0.
  refused if    no drive clears both at once, or the drive axis simply
                reproduces the gain axis's monotone trade. That would make
                the negative complete in BOTH dimensions of the window and
                say the trade belongs to the architecture, not the axis.
  liveness      `voiced` is the voiced frame fraction. A drive outside the
                oscillating window silences the voice, and a silent
                creature has no lesson to lose -- so a null there is a
                BOUND on the window, not a failure of teaching.


